Subject: [PATCH 4/4] wifi: brcmfmac: skip reset-work cancellation before initialization

Match the schedule-side initialization check under bus_reset_lock. Attach
failure can leave drvr present before INIT_WORK; cancel_work_sync then warns.
Do not change successful-attach work initialization or scheduling behavior.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c
@@ -1184,7 +1184,7 @@
 {
 	mutex_lock(&bus_if->bus_reset_lock);
 	bus_if->removing = true;
-	if (bus_if->drvr)
+	if (bus_if->drvr && bus_if->drvr->bus_reset.func)
 		cancel_work_sync(&bus_if->drvr->bus_reset);
 	mutex_unlock(&bus_if->bus_reset_lock);
 }
